# 5. REMAINING ROADMAP TO LAUNCHABLE PLATFORM

---

# PHASE 1 — REAL ENGINE LOOP

## Goal

Connect live Unity runtime into TRT semantic bridge.

---

## Required

### 1. Unity Runtime Client

#### Needs

* live runtime event posting
* runtime session state
* telemetry streaming
* deterministic bridge formatting

#### Challenges

* WebGL limitations
* async state synchronization
* Unity networking lifecycle
* reconnect handling

#### Decision

Unity remains telemetry/input-only initially.

No autonomous dispatch.

---

### 2. Session Identity System

#### Needs

* Firebase Auth
* session ownership
* profile linkage
* anonymous upgrade flow

#### Challenges

* Unity ↔ web session synchronization
* reconnect stability
* runtime ownership consistency

#### Decision

Session ownership becomes mandatory before persistence.

---

### 3. Live Bridge Stream

#### Needs

* live event intake
* throttling
* runtime buffering
* event deduplication

#### Challenges

* bridge spam
* runtime loops
* semantic flooding

#### Decision

Introduce rate limiting before enabling live gameplay telemetry.

---

# PHASE 2 — PERSISTENT PLATFORM

## Goal

Convert temporary runtime into real platform state.

---

## Required

### 4. Event Persistence Layer

#### Needs

* BridgeEvent storage
* Session history
* Recognition history
* Semantic outcomes

#### Challenges

* schema evolution
* replay determinism
* scaling event volume

#### Decision

Persistence must remain replay-safe and audit-safe.

---

### 5. PowerStarter Feed Integration

#### Needs

* progression feed
* achievements
* recognitions
* milestone rendering
* journal system

#### Challenges

* meaningful progression UX
* avoiding shallow gamification

#### Decision

PowerStarter owns user-visible progression output.

---

### 6. GMS Runtime Control Layer

#### Needs

* feature gates
* route approvals
* runtime governance
* semantic overrides

#### Challenges

* governance complexity
* operator usability

#### Decision

GMS owns:

* routing
* approval
* governance decisions

NOT semantic evaluation ownership.

---

# PHASE 3 — UNITY WEB ENGINE

## Goal

Deliver the first real TRT engine experience.

---

## Required

### 7. Unity WebGL Engine

#### Needs

* `/engine`
* embedded Unity runtime
* live bridge connectivity

#### Challenges

* browser memory limits
* WebGL performance
* websocket/runtime stability

#### Decision

WebGL becomes the first launchable engine surface.

---

### 8. Semantic Visualization

#### Needs

* graph overlays
* route chains
* semantic relationships
* pattern inspection

#### Challenges

* visual overload
* complexity explosion

#### Decision

Visualization must remain layered and inspectable.

---

### 9. Design Book Integration

#### Needs

* centralized design tokens
* runtime theming
* semantic visual states

#### Challenges

* inconsistent UI systems
* scaling component architecture

#### Decision

Design Book becomes the canonical visual governance layer.

---

# PHASE 4 — CONTROLLED AUTOMATION

## Goal

Enable approved semantic actions safely.

---

## Required

### 10. Candidate Approval System

```text
event
→ semantic evaluation
→ candidate proposal
→ governance approval
→ Unity action
```

#### Challenges

* infinite loops
* unsafe runtime behavior
* nondeterministic orchestration

#### Decision

No automatic dispatch without:

* governance review
* replay validation
* audit confirmation

---

### 11. Semantic Scoring

#### Needs

* confidence
* priority
* recognition strength
* route weighting

#### Challenges

* noisy semantic output
* overfitting
* unexplained behavior

#### Decision

All semantic scoring must remain explainable and inspectable.

---

# PHASE 5 — LAUNCHABLE PLATFORM

## Goal

Convert engineering runtime into real product.

---

## Required

### 12. UX & Product Polish

#### Needs

* onboarding
* progression clarity
* responsive runtime UX
* visual consistency

#### Challenges

